config SPRD_PDBG
	tristate "Spreadtrum power debug (wakeup / sleep logging)"
	depends on ARM64 && PROC_FS && PM
	select SPRD_SIP_SVC
	help
	  Explains why the SoC slept or woke up: matches the wakeup-source
	  irq-domain names from the debuglog device tree node against the
	  live irq descriptors, logs the active wakeup sources from a
	  kernel thread, records suspend duration from the PM notifiers and
	  pulls sleep statistics from the SIP power service
	  (pwr_get_pdbg_info, SMC 0x82000502).

	  Exports sprd_pdbg_msg_print() for other drivers and
	  /proc/sprd-pdbg/regs_info for the register snapshot.

	  Port of the vendor 5.4 `sprd_pdbg.ko`.
